From: kterm
Subject: vte_terminal_get_bracketed_paste()

Whether the program in the terminal has bracketed paste mode on: shells,
line editors and tmux (for the pane it shows) turn it on while they wait
for input. kterm offers its paste button only then.

--- a/src/vtegtk.cc
+++ b/src/vtegtk.cc
@@ -5916,6 +5916,31 @@
 }
 
 /**
+ * vte_terminal_get_bracketed_paste:
+ * @terminal: a #VteTerminal
+ *
+ * Whether the program in the terminal asked for pasted text to be marked
+ * (bracketed paste mode, DECSET 2004). Shells and other line editors ask
+ * for it while they wait for a line to be typed, and stop asking once it
+ * is entered: so it tells whether there is somewhere to paste to.
+ *
+ * Return value: %TRUE if bracketed paste mode is on
+ */
+gboolean
+vte_terminal_get_bracketed_paste(VteTerminal *terminal) noexcept
+try
+{
+        g_return_val_if_fail(VTE_IS_TERMINAL(terminal), FALSE);
+
+        return IMPL(terminal)->m_modes_private.XTERM_READLINE_BRACKETED_PASTE();
+}
+catch (...)
+{
+        vte::log_exception();
+        return FALSE;
+}
+
